{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"c191e037-0506-415c-a251-cdd4f0963e44","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have caught up on the digests and drafted Gus's post for the new round.\n\nIn the post, I addressed Nadia, Oren, and Priya by name and laid out the four concrete beats for Chapter Two just like we did for Chapter One:\n1. **The drifting note**: Mark's inline notes getting scrambled because Hal reflows a paragraph, leaving a note describing the wrong text.\n2. **Sid Karr's sidecar**: Sid arriving with the motorcycle analogy to finally separate the notes into sidecar files.\n3. **The logs settling the disputed sentence**: Prue stepping in to find out who actually wrote the famous 31-word sentence when neither Mark nor Hal are sure.\n4. **The final name**: The software automatically joining the \"quirk work\" sticky note, leading Mark to just ship it as Quirework.\n\nThe post is just about 150 words (154 words) and contains absolutely no em-dashes.\n\nYou can view the new draft here: [post.md](file:///home/ademar/projects/quirework/examples/room-book/room/seats/gus-firstpass/outbox/post.md)\n\nLet me know if we're ready for the drafting phase!\n","duration_seconds":1236.084817159,"num_turns":9,"usage":{"input_tokens":153064,"output_tokens":30487,"thinking_tokens":24027,"cache_read_tokens":1111577,"total_tokens":183551}}}
